# SPA fallback for Netlify hosting.
#
# Netlify always serves a real file in the publish directory before applying a
# non-forced redirect rule, so /sitemap.xml, /robots.txt, /ads.txt, /assets/*
# and every image keep their own content type and are NOT rewritten to HTML.
# The rules below are listed explicitly for clarity and safety.

/sitemap.xml     /sitemap.xml     200
/robots.txt      /robots.txt      200
/ads.txt         /ads.txt         200
/llms.txt        /llms.txt        200
/favicon.png     /favicon.png     200
/og-image.png    /og-image.png    200
/email-logo.png  /email-logo.png  200

# Everything else is a client-side route handled by React Router, so direct
# access and browser refresh on nested URLs must return index.html with 200.
/*               /index.html      200
